4. `wayfinde{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"ec9b56bf-6205-4a61-9d59-f68dfbdecbe7","status":"SUCCESS","response":"# Functionality Understanding Check (`INV-ALIGN-01`)\n\n**Governing Functional Specification:** [functional_specification_004.md](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-20261013T025302-800-gxuw/functional_specification_004.md)  \n**Taxonomy Authority:** [LANGUAGE.md](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-20261013T025302-800-gxuw/LANGUAGE.md)  \n**Run ID:** `20261013T025302-800-gxuw`  \n**Evaluation Role:** Planning Node (`wayfinder-read-and-plan`)\n\n---\n\n## 1. Articulation of Desired `{functionality}`\n\nThe objective of [functional_specification_004.md](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-20261013T025302-800-gxuw/functional_specification_004.md) is to architect, plan, and specify the implementation of an end-to-end browser-based React graph visualization interface coupled with an integrated Hugging Face **Graph-Augmented Retrieval Generation (GraphRAG)** conversational intelligence engine operating across multi-tier policy property graphs (e.g., LTA, IVIG).\n\nThe target system comprises three natively synchronized operational capabilities:\n1. **Interactive Browser Graph Canvas:**\n   - Visualizes all 14 node entity types (`Policy`, `Bill`, `PublicLaw`, `StatutorySection`, `Regulation`, `ChangeRequest`, `CoveragePolicy`, `HCPCSCode`, `ICD10Code`, `Jurisdiction`, `State`, `FeeScheduleEntry`, `LobbyingFiling`, `LiteratureStudy`) and all 14 directed relationships.\n   - Enforces visual hierarchy with distinct colors, shapes, and badges, displaying human-readable `name` properties instead of raw internal system identifiers.\n   - Provides force-directed layout navigation (pan, zoom, fit-to-screen, dragging) with pause/lock physics simulation controls.\n   - Employs scalable clustering/summarization for high-cardinality tiers (specifically 3,800+ `:FeeScheduleEntry` nodes) to lock a 60 FPS viewport.\n   - Features a dedicated detail drawer showing entity primary keys, official titles, descriptions, first-class properties, direct government source URLs (e.g., GovInfo, Federal Register, eCFR, CMS MCD), and immediate relationship navigation.\n\n2. **Hugging Face GraphRAG Engine:**\n   - Strictly eliminates bespoke per-question Cypher code generation and LLM Cypher syntax hallucinations.\n   - **Stage 1 (Entity Anchor Linking):** Deterministically resolves unstructured user prompts into indexed graph anchors (`State`, `ICD10Code`, `Policy`) via lexical matching and clinical lay synonym mapping (`INV-FAIL-FAST`).\n   - **Stage 2 (Generalized Subgraph Expansion):** Executes generalized topological path traversal ($k=1$ to $3$ hops) linking state, regional contractor (`Jurisdiction`), authorizing directive (`ChangeRequest`), coverage policy (`CoveragePolicy`), procedure codes (`HCPCSCode`), diagnosis codes (`ICD10Code`), and local reimbursement rates (`FeeScheduleEntry`). Strictly adheres to `INV-NO-KEYWORD-BRIDGING`.\n   - **Stage 3 (Structured Context Assembly):** Formats retrieved subgraphs and edge provenance metadata into structured Markdown factual blocks.\n   - **Stage 4 (Hugging Face Model Synthesis):** Synthesizes plain-English grounded responses via Hugging Face open-weight instruction models (e.g., Llama-3-8B-Instruct, Mistral-7B-Instruct) with zero hallucination.\n   - **Stage 5 (Mandatory Provenance Citation):** Cites edge provenance metadata (`source_uri`, `selector`, `ingestion_timestamp`, `run_id`) in every factual statement (`INV-PROVENANCE-COMPLETENESS`).\n\n3. **Bidirectional Canvas-Agent Synchronization Bus:**\n   - Canvas-to-Agent: Selecting a node or edge seeds active anchors in the GraphRAG pipeline and surfaces quick-action prompts.\n   - Agent-to-Canvas: GraphRAG emits active node IDs and edge keys; the canvas illuminates the active path, attenuates unrelated nodes to 20% opacity, and interpolates camera pan/zoom within 350ms.\n\n4. **Deterministic User Workflows:**\n   - **Workflow 1:** Natural Language Patient Benefit Routing (*\"I am from Wisconsin, survived breast cancer, need lymphedema supplies, I'm on Medicare\"* $\\rightarrow$ resolves `STATE-WI`, `ICD10-I97.2`, `POLICY-LTA`, DME MAC B, `A6522`, fee rate $290.47, 20% coinsurance $58.09, and illuminates 7-node path).\n   - **Workflow 2:** Clinical Coverage \u0026 Diagnosis Bridging (verifies `CoveragePolicy` as mandatory legal intermediary).\n   - **Workflow 3:** Cross-Policy Comparative Lineage (`POLICY-IVIG` and `POLICY-LTA` shared omnibus enactment under `PLAW-117-328` and `FR-2023-24455`).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Standard Evaluation Parameters Assessment (`LANGUAGE.md`)\n\n- **`{errors}`:** No errors or ambiguities identified in the upstream specification. Empirical verification confirms Neo4j graph storage is active with 3,971 nodes and complete relationships across all 5 tiers.\n- **`{correctness}`:** The specification's composite primary keys, schema entities, relationship labels, and provenance contracts match existing models in [src/graph/models.py](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-20261013T025302-800-gxuw/src/graph/models.py) and data exports in [exports/](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-20261013T025302-800-gxuw/exports/).\n- **`{functionality}`:** The desired system behavior provides an integrated exploration experience connecting patient lay language to federal statutory, regulatory, and reimbursement realities with verifiable provenance and visual synchrony.\n- **`{correct required outputs}`:** The planning phase must generate:\n  1. Updated Wayfinder roadmap at [wayfinder/20261013T025302-800-gxuw/map.md](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-20261013T025302-800-gxuw/wayfinder/20261013T025302-800-gxuw/map.md).\n  2. Monotonically numbered decision tickets in [wayfinder/20261013T025302-800-gxuw/tickets/](fi